    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0373" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg313"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Is the French proposition that Waller be released; that such release close the
                    incident as between the two Governments, leaving Waller the same rights and
                    remedies before French tribunals as would, under the like circumstances, be
                    available to a Frenchman?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
